{{Quote|During a walk around the city, I was startled when a leaf started a conversation with me! However, upon closer inspection I realized it was actually an Ishi Tib....|An entry of an artist's journal|<ref name="AlienArchive" />}}
'''Ishi Tib''' were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] of [[Amphibian|amphibious]] [[humanoid]]s from the [[planet]] [[Tibrin]]. They had skin that ranged from [[Color|green]] to blue, large [[eye]]s that extended from angular stalks on either side of their skull, and a [[Beak|beak-like]] [[mouth]]. A number of Ishi Tib were employed for [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure|Jabba]] the [[Hutt]], while others fought for the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]].

==Biology and appearance==
[[Homeworld|Hailing]] from the [[planet]] [[Tibrin]], Ishi Tib were [[Sentience|sentient]] [[Amphibian|amphibious]] [[humanoid]]s.<ref name="AlienArchive" /> The species [[Reproduction|reproduced]] by laying [[egg]]s. Once fertilized, these eggs were cared for in communal hatcheries carved into sandbars near the coral reefs that supported their settlements. Reproduction was seldom carried out for personal reasons, as eggs were fertilized only when the community required it. For six years, the eggs remained under collective care until the young were capable of leaving the [[water]]. Due to the communal nature of child rearing, Ishi Tib never knew who their parents were.<ref name="Lead By Example FFG" />

[[File:IshiTibGuildMaster-BoBFCh5.png|thumb|left|180px|At least [[Unidentified Ishi Tib guild master|one]] Ishi Tib sported blue skin]]
The species sported a [[Beak|beaked]] [[Mouth|mouth]] and [[Eye|eyestalks]] protruding from its star-shaped face.<ref name="AlienArchive" /> Their skin was leathery<ref name="Lead By Example FFG" /> and often green in coloration,<ref name="AlienArchive" /> although they were also sometimes blue.<ref name="Return of the Mandalorian" /> Their eyes were commonly yellow and with vertically-slitted pupils, though other colored eyes such as orange and yellow-green have been recorded. An Ishi Tib's face featured two pouch-like cheeks that they used to store [[Foodstuff|food]] such as [[algae]], microscopic organisms and [[crustacean]]s.<ref name="Lead By Example FFG" /> Although commonly used to crack the exoskeletons of their live food, some Ishi Tib also used their beaks as a [[weapon]].<ref name="Lead By Example FFG" />

Ishi Tib had a very acute sense of smell, and were able to use it on land and underwater.<ref name="AlienArchive" /> Their [[Limb|hands]] varied, some had short, thick, almost stumpy mitten-like appearances,<ref name="Episode VI" /> while others could have extended, three-digited, flipper-like hands.<ref name="Guns for Hire">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 22: Guns for Hire}}</ref> They had fin-like feet which allowed for agile swimming.<ref name="Lead By Example FFG" /> Despite having a thick skin that minimized water loss, to stay healthy, they had to regularly submerge themselves in a saline solution that was similar to the waters of Tibrin. Without this submersion, dehydration could quickly set in, leading to severe debilitation or death within days.<ref name="Lead By Example FFG" /> At least one Ishi Tib possessed a tail.<ref name="Leia2015-2">[[Princess Leia 2|''Princess Leia'' 2]]</ref> 

==Society and culture==
Ishi Tib were native to the oceanic planet of Tibrin,<ref name="AlienArchive" /> having built settlements situated atop the world's waves<ref name="Trouble at Tibrin" /> and coral reefs.<ref name="AlienArchive" /> Ishi Tib society was organized into large communities known as "schools", each numbering up to 10,000 individuals. Every school was governed by an elected representative who served a one-year term. [[Ecological Law|Ecological Law]] placed the preservation of nature above all other concerns.<ref name="Lead By Example FFG" /> [[Tibrina]], Tibrin's [[capital]] [[city]], was one such settlement. It was located at least partially above the surface of the ocean.<ref name="Trouble at Tibrin">{{IDWAdventuresCite-2017|issue=4|story=The Trouble at Tibrin}}</ref>

[[File:GoviAndIshiTib.png|thumb|left|320px|Two Ishi Tib on Tibrin]]
Ishi Tib were cautious of new technologies, with all new devices and scientific processes were reviewed and regulated according to [[Ecological Law|ecological law]]. The species had a culture highly aware of its environmental impact. Because of these restrictions, many offworld corporations had chosen not to conduct business with Tibrin.<ref name="Lead By Example FFG" /> Tibrin was [[Tibrin government|administrated]] by a [[Mariod]] and received spiritual guidance from a [[Kalikeedan]], an eminent local [[Religion|religious]] figure.<ref name="Kalikeedan tweet">{{Twitter|LandryQWalker|status/936267479789158400|[[Landry Q. Walker|Landry Quinn Walker]]|quote=On the subject of the Ishi-Tib: Mariod isn't a name, it's a title - essentially a high ranking governor. The Kalikeedan is the planet's highest ranking spiritual leader.|nobackup=1}}</ref>

The species was most comfortable underwater.<ref name="VE" /> Ishi Tib spoke a [[language]] called [[Ishi Tibrin]], also known as "Tibranese," which consisted of squeals, honks and clicks. This language also served as the basis for [[Tibranese hieroglyphics]].<ref name="Lead By Example FFG" /> Among the Ishi Tib, opening ones beak without a sound was the equivalent of a [[human]] frown.<ref name="Moving Target">''[[Moving Target: A Princess Leia Adventure]]''</ref> The species while generally quite mild mannered and not known to act rashly, yet they had acquired a reputation for snapping violently under extreme stress. When confronted by enemies or hostile circumstances, they entered a state of uncontrolled rage, in which instinct rather than reason had guided their actions.<ref name="Lead By Example FFG" />

==History==
Ishi Tib evolved from large [[Bone|bony]] [[fish]] that lived in the [[coral]] reefs of their home planet.<ref name="Lead By Example FFG">[[Lead by Example]]</ref> Ishi Tib were seen in the wider galaxy by [[382 BBY]].<ref name="THRDate">''[[Star Wars: The High Republic Character Encyclopedia]]'' dates the events of ''The High Republic'' (2022) 5 to [[382 BBY]].</ref> The species was represented in the [[Galactic Senate]].<ref name="Episode II">{{Film|II}}</ref>

==Ishi Tib in the galaxy==
[[File:Ishi tib.png|thumb|right|240px|An Ishi Tib [[lieutenant]] of the [[New Republic Defense Fleet]]]]
Most Ishi Tib did not leave their homeworld. Those who did were highly sought after by other governments and corporations. Their aptitude for overseeing complex projects had made them especially sought after as tacticians, executives, project managers, planners, and accountants.<ref name="Lead By Example FFG" /> However, some Ishi Tib worked in criminal professions, such as [[Pirate|piracy]]<ref name="A Test of Strength">{{TCW|A Test of Strength}}</ref> or in the employ of [[crime lord]]s.<ref name="AEYNTK">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref> [[Unidentified Ishi Tib pirate|One]] such Ishi Tib was a member of the [[Ohnaka Gang]].<ref name="A Test of Strength" /> Another, [[Benjar Pranic]], served in the [[Silvo's pirates|pirate crew]] of [[Captain]] [[Jod Na Nawood|Silvo]] during the [[New Republic Era]].<ref name="Very Interesting">{{SkeletonCrew|Very Interesting, As an Astrogation Problem}}</ref> A [[Unidentified Ishi Tib pirate (Silvo's pirates)|second Ishi Tib]] also served with Silvo. Both that pirate<ref name="SC 101">{{SkeletonCrew|This Could Be a Real Adventure}}</ref> and Pranic supported [[First Mate]] [[Brutus]]'s mutiny against Silvo.<ref name="Very Interesting" /> Shasa Tiel worked for [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure|Jabba]] the [[Hutt]].<ref name="AEYNTK" /> Another was seen on Jabba's Sail Barge the [[Khetanna]] during the [[Rescue of Han Solo]]<ref name="Episode VI">{{Film|VI}}</ref> The Ishi Tib [[Pendewqell]] worked for [[Sidon Ithano]].<ref name="Corsair">"[[The Crimson Corsair and the Lost Treasure of Count Dooku]]"</ref> One Ishi Tib criminal was located on [[Lothal]] and was shot by the Imperial [[Lieutenant]] [[Jenkes]]<ref name="Ezra's Gamble">''[[Ezra's Gamble]]''</ref> in 5 ABY.<ref name="EzrasGambleDate">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of ''[[Ezra's Gamble]]'', which includes the [[death]] of the [[Ishi Tib]] on [[Lothal]], to [[5 BBY]].</ref> On the ringed [[space station]] [[Glavis Ringworld]] there was an Ishi Tib who was the master of a guild.<ref name="Return">{{BOBF|Chapter 5: Return of the Mandalorian}}</ref> In 0 ABY,<ref name="DateSW2015-8">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of ''Star Wars'' (2015) 8 to [[0 ABY]].</ref> an Ishi Tib was present at a [[Unidentified bar (Nar Shaddaa)|bar]] on [[Nar Shaddaa|Nar Shadda]], he was surprised when Jedi Knight [[Luke Skywalker]] drew his lightsaber.<ref name="SW2015-8">[[Star Wars (2015) 8|''Star Wars'' (2015) 8]]</ref>

Waks Burr was a patron<ref name="AOTC">{{Film|II}}</ref> of the [[Outlander Club]] in the [[Uscru Entertainment District]] of the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]]<ref name="Coruscant">{{EncyclopediaCite|Coruscant (booklet)}}</ref> in [[22 BBY]].<ref name="Date">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of {{Film|II}} to [[22 BBY]].</ref> [[Waks Trode]] was present in the [[Galaxies Opera House]] in the [[Uscru District]] of Coruscant during a performance of the [[opera]] ''[[Squid Lake]]''.<ref name="USWNE">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> [[Mich Matt]] was an Ishi Tib technician that was kidnapped by the Empire to work on a secret project but was rescued by the young rebel [[Ezra Bridger]].<ref name="INR">{{Rebels|In the Name of the Rebellion}}</ref>

Many Ishi Tib worked in more legitimate environments. Of these, [[Gume Saam]] was a [[senator]] representing the [[Techno Union]] in the [[Galactic Senate|Republic Senate]]<ref name="heroes">{{TCW|Heroes on Both Sides}}</ref> while [[Gani Riduli]] represented the [[InterGalactic Banking Clan|Banking Clan]] in the [[Imperial Senate]].<ref name="TCC">{{TBB|The Clone Conspiracy}}</ref> [[Govi]] served as the [[Mariod]] of Tibrin in the early period of the [[Galactic Civil War]].<ref name="Trouble at Tibrin" /> An Ishi Tib, [[Ral Garas]], served as an advisor to [[King]] [[Amand]] of the [[planet]] [[Molos]].<ref name="Lead By Example FFG" /> During the Galactic Civil War, some Ishi Tib fought for the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]],<ref name="Battlefront">''[[Star Wars Battlefront]]''</ref> including [[Volk Aymeric]], who [[captain|captained]] an [[Remembrance|EF76 Nebulon-B escort frigate]].<ref name="Moving Target" /> Many Ishi Tib who joined the Rebel Alliance were greatly admired for their tactical prowess.<ref name="Lead By Example FFG" /> Four Ishi Tib,<ref name="Episode VI" /> including [[Vek Drow]]<ref name="CheeDiscord">{{WookDiscord|discordname=.holocronkeeper|name=Leland Chee|date=2025-04-01|messagelink=https://discord.com/channels/397848917036761090/492457166771322881/1356665374845829290|quote=For example, I decided that Vek Drow is an Ishi Tib in Return of the Jedi. Were they at Mos Eisley for the Boonta Eve race? Who knows. But at least that RotJ character has  a name.|archivefile=File:LelandChee-VekDrow1-Discord.png}}</reF> were present at the briefing before the [[Battle for Endor]]<ref name="Episode VI" /> aboard the [[flagship]] of the [[Rebel Alliance Navy|Alliance Fleet]], ''[[Home One]]''.<ref name="CGttSWG">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref> [[Beke Mon'z]] was an Ishi Tib operative of the [[New Republic Security Bureau]].<ref name="Free Fall">''[[Poe Dameron: Free Fall]]''</ref> At least one Ishi Tib, [[Blish]] volunteered to be a member in the [[Republic Defense Coalition]] during the [[High Republic Era]].<ref name="Tears of the Nameless">''[[The High Republic: Tears of the Nameless]]''</ref> An Ishi Tib, [[Harta]], lived in [[Black Spire Outpost]] on<ref name="Elee & Me">''[[Elee & Me]]''</ref> the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]]<ref name="TGTB">''[[Star Wars: Galaxy's Edge: Traveler's Guide to Batuu]]''</ref> and owned the [[Black Spire Station]].<ref name="Staff">{{GEStaff|Black Spire Station|area}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:IshiTibHandsPropJedi.png|thumb|right|200px|Ishi Tib hands made for Return of the Jedi]]
The Ishi Tib first appeared in [[1983]]'s [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VI ''Return of the Jedi'']], directed by [[Richard Marquand]].<ref name="Episode VI" /> The design of the species was based on a maquette sculpted by [[Chris Walas]], who stated that this maquette was his favorite of the ones he made for the film. The maquette featured a flesh-like tone compared to how Ishi Tib would eventually look.<ref name="WalasMaquetteInterview">{{YouTube|video=kHuOMeYngVM|text=Chris Walas on Designing Ishi Tib for Return of the Jedi|channel=@RegalRobot|name=Regal Robot|archivedate=20250917193801}}</ref>

During Production on the film the Ishi Tib had the production name of "Starfish".<ref name="Archeology2025" />  [[Nilo Rodis-Jamero]], a costume designer and costume artist on ''Return of the Jedi'', sketched one of the Ishi Tib Rebel Alliance members seen in the [[Home One]] briefing room.<ref name="ArtOf">''[[The Art of Star Wars Episode VI: Return of the Jedi]]''</ref> The Ishi Tib mask which was used in ''Return of the Jedi'', sculpted by [[Tony McVey]], was copied and used for other Ishi Tibs in the film<ref name="Archeology2025">{{YouTube|video=kzWqHmjdZZ0|text=BTS - Return of the Jedi's Creatures &#124; Full Panel #indianacomicconvention #starwarshistory #rotj|channel=@FanXComicConventions|name=FanX Comic Conventions}}</ref><ref name="SpinaTibEmail">{{EmailCite|email=File:TomSpinaEmailIshiTib.jpg|creator=Tom Spina|date=2025-11-04}}</ref>  Ishi Tib originally had mitten-like hands in ''Return of the Jedi'',<ref name="Episode VI" /> but when the species returned for [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''Star Wars:'' Episode I ''The Phantom Menace'']], new hand molds were made that replaced them with the flipper-like hands,<ref name="The Phantom Menace" /> with all subsequent live-action Ishi Tib following suit.<ref name="Shadow Warrior" /> The Ishi Tib made for ''The Phantom Menace'' all had a second face on the back of their respective mask to use as a second species.<ref name="SpinaTibEmail" /> [[Canon|Canonically]], the Ishi Tib were first identified in the episode guide for the ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' episode "[[A Test of Strength]]."<ref name="Guide">{{SW|url=explore/the-clone-wars/ep507|text="A Test of Strength" - ''The Clone Wars'' Episode Guide|nolive=1}}</ref>

